{"step_index":952,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-23T00:11:57Z","thinking":"The task involves preserving all rows in the dataset, which means no row deletion. The next step focuses on data cleaning: identifying and clearing invalid entries in phone number fields and handling other missing data by filling blank cells with a specified color. This requires identifying empty cells in the relevant columns.\n\n\nIdentifying appropriate Excel colors for \"갈색\" (brown) involves exploring standard palettes and their lighter shades.  Accent 2 (`ED7D31`, orange/brown) and its tints offer options like `#F8CBAD`, a soft warm brown/tan. Alternatively, investigating Accent 6 variants and light shades of brown is warranted for potential alternatives. The appropriate light shade or warm brown fill depends on context and readability requirements within the spreadsheet.\n\n\nIdentifying \"없는 전화번호\" means finding empty cells in the \"연락처\" column (Col 8). Also, should I consider empty fax numbers (\"팩스번호\", Col 9) to be within the scope?\n\n\"없는 데이터\" requires determining which columns contain crucial company information. Based on the data, columns like \"사업자번호\", \"대표자 성함\", \"주소\", \"종사자수\", and \"매출액\" are essential.\n\nEmpty cells needing brown highlighting are in the following columns: \"연락처\", \"사업자번호\", \"대표자 성함\", \"주소\", \"종사자수\", and \"매출액\". There are 254 empty \"연락처\" cells and 222 empty \"사업자번호\" cells.\n\n\nThe initial interpretation of \"갈색 채우고\" as filling *all* empty cells is potentially misleading; some empty cells, such as \"closed date\" for active companies, should remain blank.  The user's intent is clarified as addressing missing phone numbers and data: either filling the *cells* with missing information with brown, or highlighting the rows with missing data.\n\n\"없는전화번호다진워라\" likely means to erase dummy phone number values like \"-\", \"없음\", or \" \" found during the initial inspection.  Further analysis is necessary to determine the precise scope of \"없는 데이터\" and implement the highlighting effectively. I'll test to see both cell filling and row highlighting.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"const fs = require('fs');\n\nfunction parseCSV(content) {\n  const rows = [];\n  let currentRow = [];\n  let currentField = '';\n  let inQuotes = false;\n  for (let i = 0; i < content.length; i++) {\n    const char = content[i];\n    const nextChar = content[i + 1];\n    if (char === '\"') {\n      if (inQuotes && nextChar === '\"') {\n        currentField += '\"';\n        i++;\n      } else {\n        inQuotes = !inQuotes;\n      }\n    } else if (char === ',' && !inQuotes) {\n      currentRow.push(currentField);\n      currentField = '';\n    } else if ((char === '\\r' || char === '\\n') && !inQuotes) {\n      if (char === '\\r' && nextChar === '\\n') i++;\n      currentRow.push(currentField);\n      if (currentRow.some(f => f.trim() !== '')) rows.push(currentRow);\n      currentRow = [];\n      currentField = '';\n    } else {\n      currentField += char;\n    }\n  }\n  if (currentField !== '' || currentRow.length > 0) {\n    currentRow.push(currentField);\n    if (currentRow.some(f => f.trim() !== '')) rows.push(currentRow);\n  }\n  return rows;\n}\n\nconst csvPath = 'C:/Users/lg/Desktop/Today/(안상숙)(STI)_(모집단현행화)_부산정보산업진흥원_2026_부산_CT산업_실태조사_260910_크레탑_배현명_최종제출본.csv';\nconst content = fs.readFileSync(csvPath, 'utf8');\nconst rows = parseCSV(content);\nconst header = rows[0];\n\nconsole.log('=== CHECKING PLACEHOLDERS AND HYPHENS ACROSS ALL CELLS ===');\n\nconst found = [];\nrows.slice(1).forEach((r, idx) => {\n  const rowNum = idx + 2;\n  const name = r[2];\n  r.forEach((f, c) => {\n    const val = f.trim();\n    if (val === '-' || val === '--' || val === '없음' || val === '미등록' || val === 'null' || val === 'N/A') {\n      found.push({ rowNum, name, colName: header[c], colIdx: c, val });\n    }\n  });\n});\n\nconsole.log(`Found ${found.length} placeholder cells:`);\nfound.forEach(item => {\n  console.log(`Row ${item.rowNum} [${item.name}] Col ${item.colIdx} (${item.colName}): [${item.val}]`);\n});\n","Description":"Find all placeholder values in all cells","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\lg\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\a97462f9-3976-4927-b799-281f20134eb3\\scratch\\find_all_placeholders.js","toolAction":"Write find_all_placeholders.js","toolSummary":"Write find_all_placeholders.js"}}]}
